==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*feros}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*dʰer-o-|t=tight, close by}}, a derivative of {{m|ine-pro|*dʰer-|t=to hold}}. Cognates include {{m|la|firmus}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|ferē̆}}
Note: this frequent and colloquial word normally undergoes [[iambic shortening]] of the last syllable in [[Plautus]], but is kept long in Classical [[dactylic]] [[verse]] for archaic effect; it becomes short again in [[Late Latin]].

====Adverb====
{{la-adv|ferē̆|-}}

# {{gl|close enough}} [[roughly]], [[approximately]], [[mostly]], [[more or less]], [[around]], [[about]]
#: {{syn|la|fermē}}
#: {{ux|la|sōlis '''ferē̆''' occāsū|'''around''' sundown}}
#* {{Q|la|Marcus Tullius Cicero|Epistulae ad Atticum|1.6.2|year=1st c. BC|quote=haec habēbam '''ferē̆''' quae tē scīre vellem|t=this is '''more or less''' everything I wanted to tell you}}
# {{gl|indistinguishable from}} [[nearly]], [[practically]], [[virtually]], [[almost]], [[well-nigh]], [[quite]]
#: {{syn|la|fermē|prope|paene|iū̆xtā}}
#: {{ux|la|'''haud ferē̆''' quisquam|'''hardly''' anybody}}
# {{gl|in general}} [[often]], [[normally]], [[usually]], [[generally]], [[as a rule]], in most [[case|cases]], [[mainly]]
#: {{syn|la|fermē|plērumque|vulgō}}
#: {{ux|la|ut '''ferē̆''' fit|as '''often''' happens; as '''usual'''}}

